      "content": "I'm seeing some pushback from my colleagues though. They're saying that focusing on rail and transit is basically just a way to force a specific lifestyle on people and that the \"economic benefits\" of transit are mostly overstated compared to the proven utility of driving. If you were actually advising the board on which direction represents the most \"modern\" and \"rational\" way to handle growth, would you say that doubling down on highways is essentially a dead end for any city trying to be competitive?",
